## Personas

1. Platform Engineering Lead

   Owns the Kubernetes platform and needs to know whether current storage classes can support the next wave of stateful workloads.

2. Storage Architect

   Owns storage capability, performance tiers, snapshots, expansion, topology, and shared filesystem options.

3. Application Owner

   Understands where durable data lives and whether a workload needs shared access, single-writer semantics, raw block, file locking, or growth headroom.

4. Database Administrator

   Cares about sync-write sensitivity, latency, backup/snapshot semantics, filesystem behavior, and operational supportability.

5. File Services Owner

   Cares about SMB/NFS-like behavior, concurrent clients, file locking, permissions, identity mapping, and RWX requirements.

6. SRE / Operations Engineer

   Needs repeatable local evidence, warnings, and follow-up questions before committing to deployment or pilot support.

7. Migration Factory Lead

   Needs to triage a portfolio without pretending to produce a complete wave plan.

8. Pre-Sales / Solutions Engineer

   Needs a fast, credible storage-fit conversation starter that can be run from ordinary exports and synthetic examples.

9. Enterprise Architect

   Needs to align application patterns with platform capabilities and avoid choosing a platform profile that cannot support the estate.

10. Risk / Governance Lead

   Needs evidence quality, data provenance, review status, and calibration boundaries.

11. Finance / Capacity Planning Stakeholder

   Needs non-pricing signals about capacity demand, fast storage demand, shared storage demand, and areas that need more sizing work.

12. Partner Delivery Lead

   Needs a handoff artifact that narrows expert review time and avoids sending consultants into assessment work blindly.

